{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZc77AKTL988hik1e9bi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions in this repository:**\n- Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture with annotations (`@RestController`, `@RequestMapping`, `@PostMapping`)\n- ApiException subclasses for error handling: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n- Centralized error handling via `GlobalExceptionHandler` that converts exceptions to `ApiError` envelope\n- ErrorCode enum for machine-readable error codes\n- MockMvc for testing with `jsonPath` assertions\n\n**Affected files:**\n- `ShipmentController.kt` (lines 20-56) - Add `/confirm` endpoint\n- `ErrorCode.kt` (lines 31-37) - Need to add error code for rejected confirmations\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` (lines 23-84) - Add tests for confirm endpoint\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests\n- Incorrect idempotency handling (must not throw on already-confirmed)\n- Wrong status code for cancelled shipments\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What error code should we use for rejecting confirmation of cancelled shipments? The ticket says \"rejected with HTTP 409\" but doesn't specify the error code. I need to decide between reusing `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` or creating a new code like `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED`.\n\nLet me check if there are any patterns in how other features handle similar constraints:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":488,"cache_read_input_tokens":17267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":488},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed552468-3cdf-4b48-8927-99d08c907844","uuid":"02a5b039-31f8-4bb2-8e8e-bc560e4da89b","timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:14